WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 010, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.263
<v I_NIA>A new church, and a rate book. What did
the parish write about the Williamses?

2
00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:10.283
<v Gwen>[in Welsh] Cardiff Times, thirtieth
of December, eighteen sixty-four.

3
00:00:10.403 --> 00:00:14.263
<v Gwen>Here she is, John bach:
Amy, 'relict of the late Mr.

4
00:00:14.383 --> 00:00:16.583
<v Gwen>John Williams, Great House farm.'

5
00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:23.459
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Great House farm. Tŷ Mawr, to us.

6
00:00:23.579 --> 00:00:28.579
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Strange, seeing it in a Cardiff paper,
in English, with her name beside it.

7
00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:34.262
<v Gwen>Keep it. It shows she died a widow
and the farm went by that name.

8
00:00:34.382 --> 00:00:38.242
<v Gwen>It doesn't show who held the
ground, or on what terms.

9
00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:40.195
<v Gwen>Eighteen sixty-six now.

10
00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:45.248
<v Gwen>The new St Dochdwy's, consecrated,
and half the Vale in their Sunday best.

11
00:00:45.668 --> 00:00:49.002
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>And the old church,
put up around eighteen-twenty,

12
00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:52.722
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>taken down and carried off
to Leckwith to stand again.

13
00:00:52.842 --> 00:00:56.000
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Forty-odd years,
and off it goes on a cart.

14
00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.153
<v Gwen>That's how a local-history blog tells it.

15
00:00:59.273 --> 00:01:02.940
<v Gwen>None of us has held the
consecration papers themselves.

16
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.960
<v Gwen>Eighteen seventy-two, first of January:

17
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.641
<v Gwen>glebe land in this parish handed
over as a site for a school.

18
00:01:15.061 --> 00:01:18.928
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Which glebe? The parson's
fields run along half my hedges.

19
00:01:19.348 --> 00:01:22.614
<v Gwen>The deed's listed at
Glamorgan Archives, P35CW/9.

20
00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:26.001
<v Gwen>The catalogue line names
glebe and a school site.

21
00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:30.332
<v Gwen>It doesn't name the field,
and we've not read the deed itself.

22
00:01:30.752 --> 00:01:35.218
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>Mr Williams? Assistant overseer,
for the poor rate. Ninth of April.

23
00:01:35.338 --> 00:01:37.444
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>A moment of your time, please.

24
00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:41.730
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>I have you entered as occupier
of glebe land in Llandough.

25
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.184
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>Owner: the Reverend H. H. Rickards.

26
00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.760
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>The rate falls on you as occupier.

27
00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.741
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>So I farm the church's field and
pay the parish for the privilege.

28
00:01:52.161 --> 00:01:57.494
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>The book records who occupies and who
owns, Mr Williams. That is all it records.

29
00:01:57.914 --> 00:02:01.648
<v Gwen>So it puts John on church
glebe in eighteen seventy-two.

30
00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:06.329
<v Gwen>Not which fields, nor that any
Great House ground was his to own.

31
00:02:06.449 --> 00:02:10.649
<v Gwen>And we've the entry, not yet the
rate book's archive reference.

32
00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:16.683
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Glebe on one side, estate on the other,
and Tŷ Mawr in the middle, paying both.

33
00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:20.636
<v Gwen>And down by the river they're
talking lime and kilns.

34
00:02:20.756 --> 00:02:23.090
<v Gwen>Paper's only getting thicker, John.
